a grocery store collapse causes shock in  the central part of the valley the front  part of the la bonita building near  desert in eastern just came down this  morning leaving several people hurt  they're all expected to be okay but a  lot of people are wondering how this  could have happened in the first place  sasha loptis spoke to a local expert  tonight  a horrifying collapse turns a valley  grocery store to rubble and as i'm  backing up i see the ceiling just fall  down adolfo navarate was working inside  this central valley la ponita  supermarket when its front entrance  crashed down friday sounded like a bunch  of water just falling on top of each  other stacking just  four people were hurt but things could  have been worse so we asked civil  engineer rhonda cervantes how something  like this could happen i've seen things  that have  failed before but  not to this magnitude while no official  cause is determined she says several  things could have led to what she calls  a building facade failure it could be  you know members failing but also could  be you know connections failing or  things that get weakened over time while  design flaws a saturated roof from  recent rain or the building's age could  all be contributing factors she calls an  event like this unheard of that's why  there's such  importance in all the design factors  that we as engineers have to use to make  sure that these kind of things don't  happen as for dolfo he says it's an  experience he'll never forget it's hard  to put into words because it just  happened so suddenly and he's grateful  to have walked away to tell the story  sasha loftis 8 news now  we also reached out to the property  manager of francisco center where la  bonita is located so they issued this  statement on the collapse the safety and  security of our shoppers tenants and  employees is our top priority while we  don't have details to share at this time  as to the cause of the incident we're  working closely with our tenant and  local officials in their investigation  and la bonito issued a statement on the  collapse as well saying we have more on  that actually for you on our website at  8newsnow.com
 

